<h1><span lang="EN-GB">MMIB</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Describes some of the problems related to</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>ModelMaker Interface Box</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<h2><span lang="EN-GB">Wrong MMIB</span></h2>
<p>KUBE only supports MMIB-D, MMIB-D2, and MMIB-DL. If you are trying to use any other hardware, an error message will appear advising to upgrade your equipment to the appropriate one.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<h2>Hardware malfunctioning</h2>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If this message appears during startup, this indicates communication problems between the SURFA PCI and MMIB. The SURFA PCI, MMIB, and/or cable may be faulty.</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Check your hardware first.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Try restarting KUBE and also try pressing 'Refresh MMIB / Sensor status' button in</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;"><i><b>System &gt; Hardware Settings &gt; Calibration and Alignment</b></i></span><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Ensure the KUBE drivers are installed correctly.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
